On Fri, Aug 02, 2002 at 12:06:32PM +0200, Vakvarju wrote:
>
> I use an Adaptec 2940UW right now, so I boot from
> floppy. Unfortunately here in Hungary I did not find even used,
> second hand SCSI cards supported by SRM to make the Alpha bootable
> from HDD.

SRM on MIATA is very happy to boot from IDE devices, as most have
been sold with an IDE CDROM.

Add a small/old/cheap IDE harddisk, and partition it with BSD-style
label, install "aboot" and an initial /etc/aboot.conf and /boot
kernels/initrds, and away you go.

Just say "no" to floppy booting.

:-) :-) :-)

