The current SETI client will work on EV7's unmodified. But my attempts at optimizing the client even more than it is now haven't come anywhere near the performance I am getting out of the Itanium 2. So far at least. I haven't given up yet though! :-)

For some work loads, EV7 will not be any faster than the current EV68's. They are the same CPU core. The EV7 just has a lot of other stuff on board like the memory controller and I/O controller and the onboard L2 cache. Remember the Itanium 2 has THREE levels of cache on the chip. That helps a lot I'm sure.

I'm only talking about the SETI client here. I'm not sure if any SPEC numbers have been released for EV7 and I am not aware of what plans exist in that area (I'm not involved so I don't know).

The only EV7 I have ever played with was the Marvel that was on "Testdrive" like everyone else. And that was just a prototype so you can't judge final performance based on that anyway.

Jeff


