For a UP2000 board, you can test the memory before booting the kernel.

However, I think the original requestor wants more interesting and
rigorous testing of memory, that is, not just a sequential scan and
subsequent blessing thereof.

I think that unless something is seriously wrong, you're going to have
to wait a long time to see a bit flip from a cosmic ray.  But those cosmic
ray events will occur, if you look long enough.  I guess that's where the
ECC memory comes in.

    douglas

