Peter:

Hmmm, those messages are something worth investigating.
No, I would not attribute those messages to a cosmic ray.
Quite unlikely, but quite likely in the long run.  I had a friend
who had problems in Germany the first day of the Chernobyl
radiation disaster -- but that was a bioinformatics task
(a reading from a scintillation counter) and not ECC memory.

I have a UP2000 board and not the UP2000+ board, but I have
seen all-or-nothing problems with the memory on two occasions.
Reseating all the memory and other religious rituals fixed my
problem.  Sounds like that will not help you.  However, if
you get these errors all the time, I would rotate memory chips
and/or use a leave-one-out strategy.  Sorry I cannot be helpful.

    douglas

