Hi all!

I have a SX164 board, an ev56/533 CPU and a LSI 4140U controller. I recently
bought a Seagate 18G disk (ST318436LW) which is correctly recognised and
reported by the SRM console after powering up. But when I tried to install 7.2
the installer did not recognise the disk at all, it only reported my old 4GB
drive. Removing that drive did not help either.

After installing a second SCSI controller (Adaptec 2940) I was able to install
to the 18G drive and everything seemed fine. But as the Adaptec-controller was
not recognised by the console, I was not able to boot this new installation.
When I reconected the drive to the old LSI controller I was able to boot my
system from it, but after the kernel was loaded it was not able to mount it and
paniked.

Any ideas?

Thanks for any help,

Tom 			

-- 
