On Thursday 08 August 2002 02:32, Thomas Elmer wrote:
> Hi all!
>
> I have a SX164 board, an ev56/533 CPU and a LSI 4140U controller. I
> recently bought a Seagate 18G disk (ST318436LW) which is correctly
> recognised and reported by the SRM console after powering up. But when I
> tried to install 7.2 the installer did not recognise the disk at all, it
> only reported my old 4GB drive. Removing that drive did not help either.

Is the LSI 4140U the same as the LSI_53C1010???

>
> After installing a second SCSI controller (Adaptec 2940) I was able to
> install to the 18G drive and everything seemed fine. But as the
> Adaptec-controller was not recognised by the console, I was not able to
> boot this new installation. When I reconected the drive to the old LSI
> controller I was able to boot my system from it, but after the kernel was
> loaded it was not able to mount it and paniked.
>
> Any ideas?

I would suspect that the loadable kernel module that is needed for 
your controller is not in the /boot/initrd-2.4.9-32.5.img.  I would
try to recreate the initrd which includes the correct driver.  I suspect 
that you'll have to boot from the CD in rescue mode, and then at 
the # prompt

chroot /mnt/sysimage
mount -a
mkinitrd -f -v /boot/initrd-2.4.9-32.img 2.4.9-32
sync
reboot


which may not work if in rescue mode you can not see the HD.

So as an alternate you could rebuild the initrd by hand with

mkinitrd -f -v --preload sd_mod --preload aic7xxx --preload sym53c8xx --preload jbd --preload ext3 /boot/initrd-2.4.9-32.img 2.4.9-32

the sym53x8xx, IIRC is the driver for LSI_53C1010.

I hope this helps.

Best Regards,


--George



 




