> Besides... How do I launch a RH 7.2 install on an AlphaBios SX164? I
> haven't done this in such a long time!
> 
>    D.
> 
> 
> 
Hopefully you have a working MILO
start at the MILO prompt.

you will need two diskettes for the MILO installation process:

1. A generic installation kernel diskette, from images/generic.img on CD 1.

2. A RAM disk diskette, made from images/ramdisk.img on CD 1.

To boot from the diskette, put the generic installation kernel diskette into
the diskette drive and type in the following command:

MILO> boot fd0:

The installation program should boot, and you should be able to proceed as
normal.

available configurations: linux
(or 'halt' to return back to MILO prompt)
boot:

Type in linux and press [Enter].

Place the RAM disk diskette in the diskette drive, and then the installation
should begin.


