number of OEMs the Alpha market was fairly healthy. Unfortunately not 
enough volume was achieved.
I blame most of that on marketing droids at Digital who thought that only 
selling Windows computers counted for anything.
Selling a 64 bit Alpha running 32 bit Windows was no performance advantage 
for Alpha..
By the time Alpha Linux became viable they had already lost so much money 
on that fiasco, it was too late.



