----- Original Message -----
From: "karthikeyan" <karthikeyan@aspiresys.com>

  I have a strange problem.  I wrote a perl program for sending mails.  My
mail id is : karthikeyan@gihs.com
GIHS.COM is where I have a POP Account.  Now I am right now able to send
mails to my Yahoo, Hotmail account using sendmail but not to my GIHS one.
Why is this happening.  My program is residing in GIHS server only.

It's probably a fairly simple problem. Which server are you connecting to
when you start speaking snmp? My bet is that it is one that for some reason
GIHS doesn't trust to forward email from its clients. I know many systems
are setup like this as it is considered good policy to lock down the system.

If the messages include a FROM karthkeyan@gihs.com command, try having the
script connect to gihs.com port 25. They have an ESMTP server running there,
which most likely will let you send properly.

In general you'll want to parse the from address, connect to the smtp server
for that address, and send through that.
                        Joe




