Hi folks.

I just installed RH7.2 on a Miata (500au) and everything went perfectly 
for a while. After applying all updates and a few other packages, I 
rebooted to install another hard drive, and now I'm having severe 
ethernet problems. Restarting the interface (ifup/ifdown) works for a 
bit, but as soon as I put any significant load on it, it stops responding.

I've tried both the tulip and de4x5 modules and tried setting ewa0_mode 
from SRM to both twisted-pair and auto-negotiate.

Has anyone seen this before, or could someone offer me some advice on 
how to start tracking down a cause? I've been sitting in front of this 
machine for many, many hours now (not only for this problem, just in the 
whole install process) and my brain is starting to dribble out of my ears.

It's running really well apart from this, though ... :)

Thanks.





