I have a really weird problem with my SX164, recenly re-installed with
RH7.2.

My disk is divided in three partitions, hda1 is a FAT partition and is
supposed to hold loadlin.exe and milo.

hda2 is my linux / partition an holds linux and stuff, and hda3 is swap.

Before installing RH7.2 I was running 7.1 and it worked pretty normally. I
was able to 'ls hda2:/' in Milo and it would show files. Then I could boot
a kernel and all was fine.

NOW, if I try 'ls hda2:/' I get nothing - no error, but also no files. If
I do 'ls hda1:/', I do get the file list.

I have also copied my own 2.4.19 kernel to the hda1: partition, but I
cannot get milo to boot it! Whatever I do ('boot hda1:vmlinuz') it boots
the RH7.2 default kernel (2.4.9-32).

What is going on?

