To the list,

I have lately been plagued with bugs, including the unavailability of my
root account in KDE or the superuser file utility in my working
account.  Fortunately the damage is limited and i can "root around" in a
text shell, or su into root from a user terminal window.

However, I have been having lots of server crashes, everything freezes
up and you can't even ctrl-alt-f6 out of it.  So i shut down, fsck
things back up and maybe it works next time.

I had noticed before that some of the times in my log file were off.  I
did check again.  

EVERY time i boot the computer, the clock loses exactly 2min. 20 seconds
between initializing the random number generator and mounting the proc
file system.  

I have the CD set for RH 7.2 but don't want to upgrade until this is
fixed (or at least explained), and don't want to reformat and start from
scratch (that's for Windows users, right?)

This is too regular to be a decaying clock chip, no?  Has this happened
to anyopne else, and what did you do to fix it?  

jn

