On Tue, Aug 13, 2002 at 02:02:19PM -0500, Earl Truss wrote:
> 
> I just noticed the IRQ on this report.  I just replaced an old ISA #9GXE in 
> my AlphaServer 2100 with a Matrox Mystique PCI card.  Now it appears that 
> when the card is to switch into graphics mode, the system hangs solid and 
> must be rebooted.  I boot up to the point of switching into X before the 
> hang occurs.  I get the same hang when trying to boot into the graphic 
> install program but the text one works OK.  I believe the Mystique uses IRQ 
> 11 in an I386.  Could the IRQ in my AlphaServer be a higher number that 
> conflicts with one of the other cards?

It's not the IRQ that's causing the problem, as XFree86 has never
supported the use of interrupts from graphics cards in their servers,
even for 3D, IIRC.

The real reason is, I believe, that many, if not all, of the servers
are broken on SABLE under RH 7.2. I've had trouble on an AS2100 with
both TGA and Millennium, and am looking into the cause. Stay tuned...

 --Jay++

