I have a reasonably complex network that uses vlans and a number of ppp
clients running over l2tp. So at any time I can have over 100 interfaces
active.

I am finding that ifconfig is segfaulting on me but only after the ppp
interfaces start going up and down.

It looks like the code has a bad pointer and in tramping on memory.
Sadly it is not a simple thing to find so I am wondering if anybody out
there has seen the same problem and possibly has or knows of a fix.

