On Mon, Aug 19, 2002 at 08:30:10PM -0700, Aaron Baff wrote:
> 
> I have an AlphaServer 1000a 5/333  system, full RAM
> banks, cpu card, vga/svga pci card and pci nic. When I
> power up the system, I get nothing on the monitor, OR
> the serial terminal(serial cable w/null modem hooked
> up, correct baud and bit settings). the LCD shows:
> srom v1.2 xx    
> with xx being the various boot codes as it checks
> them. it gets to d4, makes a beep, goes to d3, makes
> several beeps. pauses, then goes right to f3 and sits
> there. In the pdf manual that I found online on
> compaq's digital site, I found a way to enable the
> fail-safe boot loader, however the processor card
> show, does not match the look of the processor card I
> have; the jumpers are in different spots. so I have
> been unable to check for fail-safe boot. I have tried
> switching the RAM around in the banks, but the same
> thing happens every time. does this sound like the
> processor or the processor card is bad? 

OK, from the docs I can see, I found the following BEEP codes:

1-1-2	ROM data path error while loading console code
1-1-4	SROM code unable to load console code
1-2-1	TOY NVRAM failure
1-3-3	No usable memory detected
(others deleted because you said yours started with 1 beep)

So, which one is it?

In addition, I found the following related to the "OCP Code" you see
in the LCD panel:

D4	Testing memory bits
D3	Testing B-cache address

F3	Bcache address line error

This looks bad; did you try reseating the CPU daughtercard, as well
as all the memory modules?

 --Jay++

