Hello,

I was wondering if anybody has had any luck running Red Hat 7.1 or 7.2
on a dual DP264 machine.  We have one with dual EV6 processors, and we
are getting kernel "Oops" messages all the time with "unable to handle
kernel paging request".  These messages appear at random, sometimes
while the kernel is booting, other times after the system is up and
running for a while.  A little more information:

We have tried just about everything on the software end to solve this
problem.  This includes installing RH 7.1 and 7.2 with stock kernels.
We obtained the source for 2.4.19 from kernel.org, and compiled with gcc
2.96 and gcc3.  We have tried re-setting and reformatting swap
partitions on two different independent disks.  We have tried replacing
the RAM with new, tested chips, and reseated all other hardware in the
box.  We are booting from the SRM console, with os_type=VMS (have also
tried os_type=UNIX).

The drives are set up as RAID-1 partitions (with /boot residing on it's
own non-raided partition on a 3rd spare disk).

If anybody has further suggestions on how to troubleshoot this thing, it
would be greatly appreciated.  Thank you for all feedback!

--
Chris




