With regards to your message at 06:42 PM 8/25/02, Marco Benton. Where you 
stated:
>the LX doesnt support more than one image in flash.  so using the AlphaBIOS
>menu to change from AlphaBIOS to SRM or vice-versa is useless.
>
>download the SRM image from DEC and rename to file to fwupdate.exe.  but
>you have to make sure you download the correct image.  it seems like you
>are downloading the AlphaBIOS image and not the SRM image.  i dont remember
>the update asking for an options disk.
>
>ftp://ftp.digital.com/pub/DEC/Alpha/firmware/archive/alphapc164lx.html


And the instructions there are:
"Download and rename firmware image to fwupdate.exe
Download the make boot utility mkbootfirm.tar.
Untar mkbootfirm on a Tru64UNIX system
# tar xvf mkbootfirm.tar
Low-level format a floppy disk:
# fddisk -fmt /dev/rfd0a
Create a bootable floppy from the downloaded firmware image:
# ./mkbootfirm fwupdate.exe | dd of=/dev/rfd0c bs=64k
Insert the bootable floppy in the target systems floppy drive, then
boot it from the SRM console: boot dva0"


And you get the mkbootfirm utility at:
ftp://ftp.digital.com/pub/digital/Alpha/firmware/archive/mkbootfirm.tar

Or, if you don't want to fiddle around email me off-list and I will send 
you an attachment copy of an OEM LX ROM image which can be installed much 
more simply.
Then, when in, you update to the newer one.
Without the above procedure it's a bit of a chicken and egg thing.
As the ROM is not big enough for both, and the website version assumes you 
are already running SRM, and merely want an update, it's difficult. The 
file which you renamed to fwupdate.exe is a TRU64 binary.


