Actually, the ROM image is already in the ftp.digital.com directory.
There is just no direct link to it.  To find the file, just browse
one of the download links without the filename...

ftp://ftp.digital.com/pub/DEC/Alpha/firmware/archive/alphapc164lx

The ROM image filename is lx164srm.rom

And Maurice is right, it's absolutely so straight forward it's
not one of the documented options.  Here's the steps:

- Download the file to a FAT formatted floppy
- Boot the Alpha
- Once booted, press F2 to go into AlphaBIOS setup
- Place aformentioned floppy in drive
- Choose AlphaBIOS upgrade and press ENTER
  and the image will be loaded from the floppy.
- A window will appear showing the information about
  the current image in flash and the new image just read
  from the floppy.
- If the new image is what you want to flash, press F10 to continue.
  Otherwise, hit ESCape to abort.

HTH,
Alan

