if you boot via "boot -fl a" or something... you can list the different
types of kernels available for boot by doing a "l" at the aboot prompt.  but
i beleive a "b -fl 0" will get you going.
 
aboot has the root and boot partition configured.  just chose a kernel to
boot.
 
so from srm you can boot the image you want,  like "boot -fl 1" boots a
serial console kernel, "boot -fl 0" boots standard with a vga card, etc...
 

