try a 'boot -fl i'

that should get you into interactive mode...Note that if you had WinNT or 
Linux installed on this before and it had DOS style partitions setup, and 
you didn't destroy the partition table before installing Linux from SRM 
there's a good chance that it won't boot at all. In this case you'll need 
to zero out the boot block and install again (or boot via floppy network 
etc...).

--rdp

P.S. Just realized you install 7.2, not sure if the above is true, is was 
for up to 7.1.

