On Tue, Aug 27, 2002 at 10:10:38AM -0400, Marco Benton wrote:

> ok...  i tried and still the same problem...  like you said, it
> seems to use the old driver.  even tho during the boot it tries the
> SYM driver first.

SYM driver doesn't handle the original 810, or any other that does NOT
have onboard memory to hold the "scripts" (read: firmware-like).

> i tried the expert command from aboot.  i thought it was suppose to
> ask me for modules to load from what i remember?  must be built-in.

Hmm; maybe you need the "noprobe" as well?

As for the original problem - is the SCSI bus split, going to the
built-in shelf up front, as well as a port out the back? If so, try
to put a terminator on the port out the back.

And please do use the RH 7.2 distro if possible; the behavior of
those kernels is most fresh in our minds... ;-}

As for how much to bother with an old EV4, well, the 4/275 is a LOT
more fun than the 4/200, especially if equipped with lots of CPUs and
a reasonable amount of memory to keep them busy, and of course the
builtin storage shelf (or two) may be full of disks... :-)

Oh, is there any chance the box has more than 1GB of memory? That may
cause problems, too, with the 2.4.9-32.5 kernel...

