> The default installation of redhat 2.4.18-3 for sendmail doesn't configure
> sendmail to receive remote mail, remote mail is refused. I read that I
> should add the option SMTPD_LISTEN_REMOTE="yes" to the configuration file.
> Does anyone know which file this is? (sendmail.cf?) I will appreciate
> any suggestions of how to correct sendmail so I remote mail could be
> received.

Finally, a question I think I might be able to answer and
even maybe get the right answer.  :-)

The file /etc/mail/sendmail.mc is what you should edit.
Then, using instructions that I think are in comments at
the head of the file, or maybe it's in a "sendmail howto"
or some similar document, you run m4 on it to create
/etc/sendmail.cf.  The .mc file is nearly comprehensible
to ordinary humans.  The .cf file is nearly indistinguishable
from binary data (except that bit 7 is always 0).  IIRC,
this option is right close to the bottom of the .mc file.

I hope I got the above right.  If not, I'm sure somebody
will correct it.

Good luck.

