On Tue, Aug 27, 2002 at 03:13:04PM -0400, Jay Estabrook wrote:
> 
> RH 7.2 install into partitions bigger than ~2GB will use a blocksize
> other than 1K (as Michal said),

I think that cut-off is much lower.  Not really sure how low but 500 or
400 Meg already will likely trigger larger blocks.  It is possible to
work-around by explicitely formatting a partition which you intend to
"show" to milo with 'mke2fs -b 1024 -O none ...' but one has to be aware
of a possible problem in the first place.

Unfortunately these are not things which you can modify with 'tune2fs'
after the fact.  This has to be reformatted.  If you can boot from CD
and you have enough of space elsewhere to store a content of '/' this
still can fixed if you will boot into ramdisk.  'tune2fs' can at least
show you your file system attributes to see if this is really a reson
for a failure.

Anaconda, i.e. a Red Hat installer, assumes (sort of in places :-) that
you are booting from SRM and if you are using milo then it may, or may
not, work but you are on your own.  Booting with milo is "not
supported".

  Michal




