> > ftp://ftp.digital.com/pub/Digital/Linux-Alpha/TESTING/sx-milo
> 
> I got the sources and binaries from
> http://www.suse.de/~stepan

It's possible that those were built with the patches I sent him, if
they were recent - the MILOs I built to do testing (in that directory
mentioned above) were dated during May of 2002, IIRC.

That new MILO may or may not solve the U2W problem, but it should
solve the blocksize > 1K problem of the older ones.

> > Workaround, again as Michal said, is a small /boot partition into
> > which the kernels/initrds are placed.
> >
> Thank you very much for this explationation. I created a 100MB boot
> partition and I can boot off the kernel on the IDE drive.

That's fine.

> Yes but with no success at all. Infact the stock kernel was broken... it
> needed some include files for compiling correctly.
> Then Milo's fs.c had problems, wanted to fix it but the copyright said it
> was Digital's and not under GPL.

Hmm, dunno about that copyright thing, I'll look into it. As I said, I
think I remember someone talking about porting MILO to the 2.4 kernels
(Stepan is prolly the only one crazy enough to try... :-), but I think
it was incomplete at best...

> Thank you for all your help, I will try and switch to SRM.

Going to SRM will not allow you to boot from the U2W, of course, as
that's not supported on the SX or LX (though the normal 2940UW is
with the latest SRM version for those boxes).

Good luck.

