With regards to your message at 08:02 AM 8/31/02, geerten kuiper. Where you 
stated:
>My PC164 needs a new CD drive. IDE appears to be significantly cheaper 
>than SCSI. Can anyone confirm that this system, with latest/last SRM 
>console, will boot and install from ATAPI CD-ROM, both for Tru64 and Linux ?
>( I believe there were performance issues with this system's IDE, but for 
>the CD drive that doesn't matter very much. Harddisk are all SCSI. )


There should not be a problem.
When we were building LX based machines we usually installed an ATAPI CDROM 
drive.
In Linux, TRU64 and so on it worked fine.
For VMS it was a bit fussy, but would work as well.
Some models of drive seem to be better for it than others.
As none of the ones we used back then exist any more it is hard to say what 
to recommend of the new ones.



